  "decision": "refine",
  "rationale": "Round 1 shows only pipelined_m can currently satisfy both constraints with low area: its sole Pareto point is pipelined_m[W=28,N=22,A=3,F=0,round,m=6] at luts_plus_ffs=2499, power_index=4.7, throughput=57.5 MSPS, max_abs_err=2^-20.85. The pipelined family is feasible but its best area is 4464, while iterative and unrolled_k cannot reach 50 MSPS (max seen 6.66 and 6.52 MSPS). The front point sits only 7.5 MSPS above the throughput floor and has ~0.85 bits of accuracy margin, so there is room to trade throughput/accuracy for lower area. Refine around this region rather than widening or adding families.",
