    "rationale": "Round 2 gave +0.0% HV with a single-point front (pipelined_m @ 2499 luts+ffs / 4.7 power); iterative and unrolled_k are dead (0 feasible in 30 evals, max ~6.5 MSPS << 50), so all remaining budget should exploit the pipelined_m region rather than widen or add families. Both active constraints have slack at the incumbent (throughput 57.5 >= 50, err 2^-20.85 <= 2^-20), and m is capped at 6 while the feasible range runs to m=7, and W is pinned at the 28 ceiling -- so lowering W and raising m is the direct route to a smaller luts_plus_ffs. Keep ~100 of the remaining 200 evals in this round; if HV is still flat after it, stop."
